DESCRIPTION:Philadelphia Parks & Recreation subcalendar\n\nAfter School Adv
 entures <br>Most Tuesdays | 4-6 p.m. | Youth 6-11 | Drop-off | $5 cash per
  child per afternoon.<br><br>Anticipated Dates: <br>Oct 13\, 20\, 27<br>No
 v 3 (No Class)\, 10\, 17\, 24<br>Dec 1\, 8\, 15\, 22\, 29 (No Class)<br><b
 r>This staff led afterschool program\, guides children on adventures in Pe
 nnypack Park. We will meet at the Pennypack Environmental Center\, then en
 joy new adventures each week. Kids can join for one\, some\, or all advent
 ures.  <br><br>Adventures are subject to change at any time\, but will be
  all-weather\, outdoor adventures with hiking\, and lots of snow/mud/soil/
 creek water. If a specific lesson/activity is scheduled\, they will do so 
 in the first hour and hike/explore in the second. <br><br>Registration req
 uired at <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://forms.gle/hTAHF4vZf
 mVpa1Kv6&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0A1xY88Y
 cMfqRfBT-KMv6X" target="_blank">https://forms.gle/hTAHF4vZfmVpa1Kv6</a> or
  PEC@Phila.gov<br><br>Questions? <a href="mailto:PEC@phila.gov" target="_b
 lank">PEC@phila.gov</a> or 215.685.0470. <br><br>Please check your email f
 or updates.<br><br>Cash only. Exact change is appreciated. We cannot accep
 t any electronic payments. <br><br>Adventures are subject to change at any
  time\, but will be all-weather\, outdoor adventures with hiking\, mud\, r
 ock climbing\, creek\, rain\, etc. <br><br>Information at Facebook.com/Exp
 lorePEC\, <a href="mailto:pec@phila.gov" target="_blank">pec@phila.gov</a>
 \, or 215.685.0470.<br>___________________________________________________
 __________________<br>PLEASE NOTE:<br>Anyone selling tickets is a scammer.
  Unsure? Send us a quick email at <a href="mailto:pec@phila.gov" target="_
 blank">pec@phila.gov</a>.<br>Everything is subject to change. Register to 
 stay up-to-date.<br>Programs are outdoors in all-weather. We recommend dre
 ssing for the weather\, physical activity\, and ticks. We encourage wearin
 g tick repellant and doing a thorough tick check after outdoor adventures.
  Ticks don&#39\;t hibernate. TICK CHECK upon return and every day after na
 ture play.<br>The center\, bathrooms\, and picnic areas are all accessible
 \, however\, the trails are rocky and uneven.<br>Free parking in the Cente
 r&#39\;s lot and street parking along Verree Road. There is a short walk o
 n paved surface from the parking lot to the Center.<br>Photos will be take
 n of participants during this program for use by the Pennypack Environment
 al Center and Philadelphia Parks and Recreation. If you wish to opt out\, 
 please let us know before the program.<br>For questions or to register by 
 phone/email. Contact us at <a href="mailto:pec@phila.gov" target="_blank">
 pec@phila.gov</a> or 215.685.0470.
LOCATION:Pennypack Environmental Center\, 8600A Verree Rd\, Philadelphia\, 
 PA 19115\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:After School Adventures
TRANSP:OPAQUE
