UID:587s3v373ab4crlk4bir0919ln@google.com
DESCRIPTION:Substance Use Prevention and Harm Reduction\n\n<br>Register at
  <a href="https://redcap.phila.gov/surveys/?s=A7FELKJWED"><u>https://redc
 ap.phila.gov/surveys/?s=A7FELKJWED</u></a>.<br><br>Losing a partner to sub
 stance use can leave a deep and lasting ache shadowed by a range of feelin
 gs such as confusion\, anger\, shame\, loneliness\, and relief. While this
  grief can be uniquely challenging\, the good news is that you don’t hav
 e to walk this journey alone.<br><br>Join a compassionate and safe space t
 o connect and heal with others. What to Expect:<br>- Open\, nonjudgmental 
 conversation<br>- Supportive community and shared stories<br>- Gentle guid
 ance and space to grieve your own way<br><br>For more information or to re
 gister\, contact Talia Jones\, MS at talia.jones@phila.gov or via call/tex
 t at 856-823-1775.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Navigating Partner Loss: Grief Support Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Substance Use Prevention and Harm Reduction
DTSTAMP:20261111T195516Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T200000
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=2TH
UID:2kc5ojh1jbmg7jr6bkaenmcb1r_R20261008T223000@google.com
DESCRIPTION:Substance Use Prevention and Harm Reduction\n\nRegister at htt
 ps://redcap.phila.gov/surveys/?s=A7FELKJWED.\n\nBring a cup of hot tea and
  a snack and enjoy meeting others who can relate to your experience. This 
 group will include sharing personal memories\, feelings\, and recent grief
 -related challenges\, as well as music\, poetry\, prayer and other words o
 f comfort and hope. Sometimes the mood may be light\, other times deeper a
 nd more reflective. All backgrounds and experiences welcome.  \n\nContac
 t Joe O'Donnell\, MSW\, MDiv\, for questions at 267-610-8041 orjoseph.e.od
 onnell@phila.gov.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Evening Teatime Grief Support Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Substance Use Prevention and Harm Reduction
DTSTAMP:20261111T195516Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T183000
