DESCRIPTION:Office of Homeless Services\n\n<p><b>Service Connection/Site Cl
 ean-ups will occur today at these Kensington locations:</b></p><ul><li>Rea
 ch St. &amp\; Allegheny Ave.</li><li>800-811 E. Allegheny Ave.</li><li>826
  Allegheny Avenue</li><li>3200 Shelbourne St. (Both sides)</li><li>3200 N
 . H Street (both sides on corner)</li><li>3254-56 Kensington Ave. (Struct
 ure/tent)</li><li>3200 Kensington Ave. (El Stop\, both sides)</li><li>3100
  Kensington Ave. (Entire block\, both sides)</li><li>1800 E. Clearfield St
 reet (both sides)</li><li>1800 E. Orleans Street (both sides)</li><li>29
 17 Kensington Ave.</li><li>2855 Kensington Ave.</li><li>2846 Kensington Av
 e.</li><li>1800 E. Hart Lane (both sides)</li><li>2900 N. Ruth St. (Both 
 corners)</li><li>2800 N. Ruth St. (Church Steps)</li><li>1800 E. Somerset
  St. (both sides)</li><li>400 Somerset St. (Both Sides)</li><li>400-300 Tu
 sculum St. (both sides)</li><li>2750-58 Kensington Ave.</li><li>2700 Kensi
 ngton Ave. (Bridge)</li><li>E. Albert St &amp\; Kensington Ave. (Corner)</
 li><li>2600 Kensington Ave. (Across from El Stop)</li><li>2500 Kensington
  Ave. (by El Stop)</li><li>2600 B. St. (by El Stop)</li><li>2700 Emerald 
 St. (Bridge)</li><li>2800 N. Helen St. (corner) </li><li>1852 E. Madison
  St.</li><li>2000 E. Sterner St. </li></ul><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p
 ><a href="https://www.phila.gov/departments/office-of-homeless-services/" 
 target="_blank"><u><u>Office of Homeless Services</u></u></a> Encampment 
 Resolution Team (ERT) staff members join the <a href="https://www.phila.g
 ov/departments/department-of-behavioral-health-and-intellectual-disability
 -services/" target="_blank"><u><u>Department of Behavioral Health and Inte
 llectual disAbility Services</u></u></a>’s (DBHIDS) Homeless Street Outr
 each Team (Outreach) and the City’s Sanitation Department to conduct Ser
 vice Connection/Site Clean-up Days.* OHS’s ERT staff schedules and lea
 ds service connection clean-ups at various selected outdoor encampment loc
 ations in Philadelphia.  <br> <br><b>How it Works </b> <br> <br>The 
 teams post signs in advance to alert people living in tents\, RVs\, makesh
 ift shelters\, or none at all\, on sidewalks\, under bridges\, in parks\,
  empty fields\, lots\, etc.\, of upcoming service days. Each service day\,
  the teams visit the encampment sites to offer individuals services\, such
  as rides to a City intake center where staff can help find shelter spac
 e\, <a href="https://www.phila.gov/departments/office-of-homeless-service
 s/documents/program-flyers/#/?table=Homelessness%2520resources%2520in%2520
 English&q=Assistance%20for%20stranded%20travelers" target="_blank"><u><u>S
 tranded Traveler Assistance</u></u></a>\, behavioral health\, drug or medi
 cal treatment\, and other similar services. The Sanitation Department team
  further assists by cleaning up accumulated trash.  <br> <br>* Servic
 e days are not the same as formal\, encampment resolutions\, which\, whi
 le social services-led\, involve many more City of Philadelphia department
 s and nonprofit partners and follow <a href="https://www.phila.gov/media/
 20220524083135/MDO-directive-70-tent-and-structure-20210803.pdf" target="_
 blank"><u><u>specific protocols regarding personal property storage\, noti
 fication\, and other requirements</u></u></a>. </p>
LOCATION:Multiple Kensington locations
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kensington Service Connections/Site Clean-ups
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Office of Homeless Services
DTSTAMP:20261111T195516Z
END:VEVENT
