 ean-ups will occur today at these Kensington locations:</b></p><ul><li>Rea
 ch St. and Allegheny Ave.</li><li>800 E. Allegheny Ave. (entire block\, bo
 th sides)</li><li>3200 Shelbourne St. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li
 >3200 H St. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>1800 E. Hilton St. (entir
 e block\, both sides)</li><li>3200 Kensington Ave. (entire block\, both si
 des)</li><li>3100 Kensington Ave. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>1800
  E. Clearfield St. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>1800 E. Orleans St
 . (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>2900 Kensington Ave. (entire block\,
  both sides)</li><li>2800 Kensington Ave. (entire block\, both sides)</li>
 <li>2900 Ruth St. (corner of block\, both sides)</li><li>2800 Ruth St. (co
 rner of block\, both sides)</li><li>2800 Helen St. (corner)</li><li>1800 E
 . Somerset St. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>400 Somerset St. (enti
 re block\, both sides)</li><li>300 Tusculum St. (entire block\, both sides
 )</li><li>400 Tusculum St. (entire block\, both sides)</li><li>2700 Kensin
 gton Ave. (under bridge\, entire block\, both sides)</li><li>2700 Emerald 
 St. (under bridge\, entire block\, both sides)</li><li>2000 Sterner St.</
 li><li>2000 Silver St.</li><li>2600 Kensington Ave. (Across from SEPTA El
  stop)</li><li>2500 Kensington Ave. (by SEPTA El stop)</li><li>2600 B. St
 . (by SEPTA El stop)</li><li>1020–1023 E. Thayer Street</li></ul><p></p>
 <p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p><a href="https://www.phila.gov/departments/
 office-of-homeless-services/" target="_blank"><u><u>Office of Homeless Ser
 vices</u></u></a> Encampment Resolution Team (ERT) staff members join the
  <a href="https://www.phila.gov/departments/department-of-behavioral-heal
 th-and-intellectual-disability-services/" target="_blank"><u><u>Department
  of Behavioral Health and Intellectual disAbility Services</u></u></a>’s
  (DBHIDS) Homeless Street Outreach Team (Outreach) and the City’s Sanita
 tion Department to conduct Service Connection/Site Clean-up Days.* OHS
 ’s ERT staff schedules and leads service connection clean-ups at various
  selected outdoor encampment locations in Philadelphia.  <br> <br><b>Ho
 w it Works </b> <br> <br>The teams post signs in advance to alert peopl
 e living in tents\, RVs\, makeshift shelters\, or none at all\, on sidewa
 lks\, under bridges\, in parks\, empty fields\, lots\, etc.\, of upcoming 
 service days. Each service day\, the teams visit the encampment sites to o
 ffer individuals services\, such as rides to a City intake center where 
 staff can help find shelter space\, <a href="https://www.phila.gov/depart
 ments/office-of-homeless-services/documents/program-flyers/#/?table=Homele
 ssness%2520resources%2520in%2520English&q=Assistance%20for%20stranded%20tr
 avelers" target="_blank"><u><u>Stranded Traveler Assistance</u></u></a>\, 
 behavioral health\, drug or medical treatment\, and other similar services
 . The Sanitation Department team further assists by cleaning up accumula
 ted trash.  <br> <br>* Service days are not the same as formal\, enca
 mpment resolutions\, which\, while social services-led\, involve many more
  City of Philadelphia departments and nonprofit partners and follow <a hr
 ef="https://www.phila.gov/media/20220524083135/MDO-directive-70-tent-and-s
 tructure-20210803.pdf" target="_blank"><u><u>specific protocols regarding 
 personal property storage\, notification\, and other requirements</u></u><
 /a>. </p>
