UID:594h2a98dqg0mqtelg6gi0rn88@google.com
DESCRIPTION:Office of Homeless Services\n\n<p><b>A Service Connection/Site 
 Clean-up will occur today at:</b></p><ul><li>Logan Circle (200 N. 19th Str
 eet)</li><li>200 N. Camac Street</li><li>1100 Ludlow Street</li></ul><b>Ab
 out Service Connection/Site Clean-up Days </b> <p><a href="https://www.p
 hila.gov/departments/office-of-homeless-services/" target="_blank"><u><u><
 u><u><u><u>Office of Homeless Services</u></u></u></u></u></u></a> Encamp
 ment Resolution Team (ERT) staff members join the <a href="https://www.ph
 ila.gov/departments/department-of-behavioral-health-and-intellectual-disab
 ility-services/" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>Department of Behaviora
 l Health and Intellectual disAbility Services</u></u></u></u></u></u></a>
 ’s (DBHIDS) Homeless Street Outreach Team (Outreach) and the City’s S
 anitation Department to conduct Service Connection/Site Clean-up Days.* 
 OHS’s ERT staff schedules and leads service connection clean-ups at vari
 ous selected outdoor encampment locations in Philadelphia.   </p><p><b>H
 ow it Works </b> </p><p>The teams post signs in advance to alert people 
 living in tents\, RVs\, makeshift shelters\, or none at all\, on sidewalk
 s\, under bridges\, in parks\, empty fields\, lots\, etc.\, of upcoming se
 rvice days. Each service day\, the teams visit the encampment sites to off
 er individuals services\, such as rides to a City intake center where st
 aff can help find shelter space\, <a href="https://www.phila.gov/departme
 nts/office-of-homeless-services/documents/program-flyers/#/?table=Homeless
 ness%2520resources%2520in%2520English&q=Assistance%20for%20stranded%20trav
 elers" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>Stranded Traveler Assistance</u><
 /u></u></u></u></u></a>\, behavioral health\, drug or medical treatment\, 
 and other similar services. The Sanitation Department team further assist
 s by cleaning up accumulated trash.  </p><p> *Service days are not th
 e same as formal\, encampment resolutions\, which\, while social services
 -led\, involve many more City of Philadelphia departments and nonprofit pa
 rtners and <a href="https://www.phila.gov/media/20220524083135/MDO-direct
 ive-70-tent-and-structure-20210803.pdf" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>
 follow specific protocols regarding personal property storage\, notific
 ation\, and other requirements</u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.  </p>
LOCATION:Multiple locations
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OHS Service Connections/Site Clean-ups
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Office of Homeless Services
DTSTAMP:20261111T195516Z
END:VEVENT
