DESCRIPTION:Philadelphia City Planning Commission\n\nThe Philadelphia City 
 Planning Commission and partner agencies are planning the city’s future\
 , long-term intercity bus station. An open house on Wednesday\, November 4
 th at the Independence Visitor Center (599 Market Street) is the next oppo
 rtunity for Philadelphians to review their progress and provide feedback.<
 br><ul><li><strong><b>When</b></strong>: Wednesday\, November 4\, 2026\, f
 rom 6 P.M. to 8 P.M.</li><li><strong><b>Where</b></strong>: Independence V
 isitor Center\, 599 Market Street\, 2nd Floor</li><li><strong><b>Meeting f
 ormat</b></strong>: This is an open-house style meeting with informational
  posters positioned throughout the room. You can arrive at any time and le
 ave whenever you wish.</li><li><strong><b>Access</b></strong>: The buildin
 g and meeting room are fully accessible. A staff member will greet you at 
 the entrance to help navigate the meeting room.</li><li><strong><b>RSVP</b
 ></strong>: You do not need to RSVP to this event.</li></ul><br>More infor
 mation about this process is at <a href="https://www.phila.gov/2026-11-02-
 an-update-on-planning-philadelphias-intercity-bus-station/">www.phila.gov/
 dpd</a>
LOCATION:599 Market St\, Philadelphia\, PA 19106\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intercity Bus Station Open House
